WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:07.900
After learning about Plant tissues, let us

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:09.540
take a look at the various types of animal

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:12.090
tissues in details.

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:14.953
In case of animals, where the body is expected

00:00:14.953 --> 00:00:17.940
to perform uncountable functions simultaneously,

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:20.792
it is obvious that, the number of tissues

00:00:20.792 --> 00:00:22.949
will also be innumerable right?

00:00:22.949 --> 00:00:25.210
So how do we study all these?

00:00:25.210 --> 00:00:27.509
Well, we don’t need to worry!

00:00:27.509 --> 00:00:31.020
For simplicity, we would prefer dividing all

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:33.220
the animal tissues into four major categories,

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:35.380
depending upon their functions.

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:38.580
Firstly, we have the one for PROTECTION, then

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:41.219
another for CONNECTION, followed by MOVEMENT

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:44.060
AND LOCOMOTION, and lastly, for TRANSMISSION

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:48.030
OF SIGNALS for quick and efficient work.

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:49.760
Based on this, we get the

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:51.180
four major types of tissues as

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:55.980
Epithelial, Connective, Muscular and Nervous!

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:58.420
So in this video, let’s begin with the first

00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:00.020
type that is epithelial tissue.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:04.700
As the name says, Epi is Above; thus epithelial

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:07.440
tissue is the one which lies ABOVE the entire

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:11.120
body, forming a protective covering.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:13.490
Along with covering the body, it also forms

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:16.080
a barrier between the various organs separating

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:17.080
them.

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:19.660
Now the structure of the epithelial tissue

00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:21.810
is quite evident from its function.

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:22.810
Yes!

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:25.471
Since it has to form a protective layer, it

00:01:25.471 --> 00:01:28.380
cannot afford to have spaces between the cells.

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:31.480
Hence, we find the epithelial tissue to have

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:34.910
tightly packed cells, forming continuous sheets.

00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:37.420
The tissue lacks intercellular spaces and

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:41.940
has extremely small amount of cementing material.

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:44.120
So every single substance that passes in or

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:47.440
out of the cells needs to cross the epithelial

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.410
layer at least once.

00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:52.500
Accordingly, the permeability of cells will

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.510
differ in various epithelia depending upon

00:01:55.510 --> 00:01:56.980
the exchange of materials.

00:01:56.980 --> 00:02:00.026
Now when we talk about all the epithelial

00:02:00.026 --> 00:02:03.370
cells in general, we need to first understand

00:02:03.370 --> 00:02:06.560
a common characteristic between them.

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:09.320
May it be any different type of Epithelia,

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:11.730
all of them will always have the cells resting

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:15.739
on a thin, fibrous, supportive membrane like structure.

00:02:15.739 --> 00:02:18.219
This is called the BASEMENT Membrane.

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:20.780
The basement membrane, apart from supporting,

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:23.290
helps to hold the cells together in a single,

00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:27.129
straight line, to form a uniform and consistent layer.

00:02:27.129 --> 00:02:30.640
Okay, so getting back to the types of Epithelia…

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:34.730
In order to study them, let’s take a simple
example.

00:02:34.730 --> 00:02:37.409
Imagine this to be a Basement Membrane.

00:02:37.409 --> 00:02:39.640
Now, depending upon the functions,

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:41.689
let’s classify them:

00:02:41.689 --> 00:02:44.890
So let’s say the first function is filtration.

00:02:44.890 --> 00:02:46.680
What kind of structure should be

00:02:46.680 --> 00:02:47.739
present according to you?

00:02:47.739 --> 00:02:48.739
Yes!

00:02:48.739 --> 00:02:52.209
It needs to be a very flat surface.

00:02:52.209 --> 00:02:55.680
So this type of epithelium is referred to

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:57.560
as Simple Squamous epithelium.

00:02:57.560 --> 00:02:59.860
Now let’s take up the next function that

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:01.290
is ABSORPTION AND SECRETION.

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:04.660
For this, obviously we would need a larger

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:06.260
surface area right?

00:03:06.269 --> 00:03:07.880
Which is why we have these tall pillar like

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:10.739
cells on the basement membrane, making up

00:03:10.739 --> 00:03:13.560
the Columnar epithelium.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:16.860
Now at times, we need the STRENGTH or support

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:19.129
along with larger surface area.

00:03:19.129 --> 00:03:22.280
In this case, we slightly change the structure

00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:24.040
to cube like cells, and form the Cuboidal

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:25.430
epithelium.

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:28.380
Lastly, we have certain organs

00:03:28.380 --> 00:03:31.719
that need SPECIALISED secretions.

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:33.960
So in such cases, we need to modify a few

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:37.170
cells that would perform secretion of specific

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:41.569
chemicals like hormones or enzymes.

00:03:41.569 --> 00:03:43.580
These are called the gland cells, and the

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:46.150
epithelium consisting of such type of cells

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:48.709
is called the Glandular Epithelium.

00:03:48.709 --> 00:03:52.999
Well, this was about the epithelial tissue in short.

00:03:52.999 --> 00:03:56.060
Now let’s meet up in the next video, where

00:03:56.060 --> 00:03:57.989
we will discuss these four types of Epithelia.

